+## §3.0.0 · a MAJOR — a `write` STOPS FIRING WHERE THE VALUE DID NOT MOVE: `triggered` and `watched` narrow together, a constraint pair at that address is no longer asked, and the two prices the ruling accepts are declared
+
+**⟶ AND THE NUMBER IN THIS HEADING IS THE ARCHITECT'S WORD AND NOT THIS PASS'S** (`strata/decisions.md` · `D-193` item 5's `Q-10`, whose default `D-195` item 2's `O-8` keeps — **the number remains the architect's word at the release act, and no pass mints it**). **THE CLASS IS SETTLED AND IT IS `MAJOR`** — a returned member's MEANING moves on a shipped verb, **and that is not smaller than a member leaving** — **`2.0.0` is spent** (this file's own generated line names it, and `scripts/publish.sh --figures` refuses on any disagreement), **so the next line by this file's own arithmetic is `3.0.0`. THIS SECTION MOVES NO OTHER BYTE: the main manifest, its five exact `optionalDependencies` pins, the six `platforms/*/package.json` versions and the three shipped documents' generated version lines all stand where `2.0.0` left them, and the bump is the release act's** (`D-124` item 3's discipline, kept by `D-190`). **A reader who sees this section at `3.0.0` is being told what the NEXT cut carries, not what a tag carries.**
+
+**THE RULING, VERBATIM** (`strata/decisions.md` · `D-193`): *"P-3 checks literal equivalence, not reference equality"*; and (`D-195`): *"Take the default on the blocker and proceed"*. **The class is this pass's reading of `D-190`'s precedent; the number is his.**
+
+**WHAT A CONSUMER ON `2.0.0` MEETS, AT EACH ENTRY POINT:**
+
+1. **`write` STOPS FIRING THE LISTENERS REGISTERED WHERE THE VALUE DID NOT MOVE.** A `write` that lands **the literal the address already stands at** answers the same record with **`triggered: []` and `watched: []`**, and no listener body runs — **at the act's address, and at every ANCESTOR of it**, because the ancestor's assembled value did not move either. **The test is on the literal and on nothing else:** `file V` then `mem V` **fires nothing** although `readTiered` moves from `file` to `mem`; a `mem V` then `file V` **fires nothing** although the `mem` version is destroyed; `-0` over `0` **fires nothing** although a reversal's judgement would call it moved. **`op` still records the landing, and a `file`-tier write still saves.**
+2. **A CONSTRAINT PAIR AT THAT ADDRESS IS NO LONGER ASKED, AND THAT IS NOT A WEAKENING.** The pass evaluates the store's returned set; the set is now empty, so no pair is asked, nothing is repaired and nothing is refused — **on the same act, and on the same evidence `D-152` already used for the registration instants** (*"a registration that writes nothing fires nothing"*).
+3. **`triggered: []` CANNOT TELL YOU *"no registration stood"* FROM *"nothing changed."*** **The member is present either way and its emptiness is the same emptiness** — `D-78`'s device does not reach this axis. **`op.before` beside `op.after` is a second reading and a partial one**: at an address that stood at two tiers `op.before.value` is the per-tier list, so the two disagree with the rule at exactly the address the rule's price lives at.
+4. **THE GUIDE'S FIRING LIST, THE RE-ENTRANCY CLAUSE AND THE NATIVE CONTRACT ARE RE-SPELLED IN THIS RELEASE, IN PLACE.** `docs/guides/package-use.md §6`'s closed list gains the value condition; `docs/specs/storeroom-js/contract.md`'s *"a listener that writes at the address it was delivered for fires itself again … nothing detects it and nothing is meant to"* **becomes conditional on a value**; and `docs/specs/storeroom-native/contract.md`'s `P-TP-8` **(a)** and **(e)** gain it in one bounded amendment, with the failure list's *"a MISSING handle where a listener's address is a prefix of the write's"* re-cut with them — **because this release is the thing that now detects one form of that sentence.**
+
+**AND WHAT DOES NOT MOVE, NAMED SO THE NARROWING IS NOT READ WIDER THAN IT IS.**
+- **THE TOUCHED ARM IS NOT NARROWED.** A registration at a node a second identical STRUCTURED write creates or purges below it is still told, because those nodes *"exist after the write and did not before"* (`D-66`). **A re-write of the same object at `['a']` still fires a listener bound at `['a','b','c']`.**
+- **THE `delete` IS UNMOVED.** Its receipt is computed on the same one predicate and answers the act's value position `true` — a delete that removes at least one version moved the value at its address — **and a delete that removed nothing still carries `triggered: []`** (`D-3`).
+- **THE JOURNAL IS UNMOVED.** A no-change write **still mints its op**, `seq` still bumps, the compaction can still drop the oldest entry, **and `rollback(opId)` still resolves the id** (`P-TP-8` (g) holds *because* the op is minted).
+- **THE `file` SAVE OF A NO-CHANGE `file` WRITE STILL RUNS** — the same bytes are rewritten and the file's mtime moves. **A durable act that moved no durable datum is the accepted cost of not re-deciding the save's eligibility in the same release.**
+- **`log` KEEPS ITS ONE `commit` ENTRY** (`[]` is never that arm's answer), **`bodyFailures` and `returnedValues` are the one shared frozen `{}` present on both**, and **`discarded` is `[]` because no body ran and therefore no raise was born** — not because a raise was lost (`D-170`).
+- **NO NAME IS MINTED, RENAMED OR REMOVED.** A `changed` flag on the record was priced and **declined** (`D-195` item 2's `O-4`), so `Object.keys` is still `["op","watched","triggered"]` and `Object.getOwnPropertyNames` still reads SEVEN.
+
+**THE CELLS THAT CARRY THIS SECTION.** `CD-1`…`CD-16` (`tests/unit/store-core/change_detection.rs` and `tests/unit/js-constraints/change-detection.test.mjs`), **with `CD-2`, `CD-3` and `CD-9` asserting the ruling's two prices as DECLARED STATES** so a later pass cannot repair them as defects; and one existing drive is **re-derived, not weakened**: `tests/e2e/json-crossing.test.mjs`'s FRESHNESS limb gives its second write a different value, because its subject is the fresh array and not a firing count. **Two Rust drives are re-derived the same way and for the same reason** (`properties.rs`'s `P-TP-8` no-tier-test and kept cells, `watched_addresses.rs`'s `S-WATCH` `(iii)`), **each now varying the value its tiers carry so the tier-independence reading it exists for survives.**
+
